A||N||9||Will||What shares a throttle body with V6 Fieros?||||1||
Z||000000||Will||08-26-2001||04:09 PM||||In an effort to rid myself of my off-idle hesitation, I recently tried changing my throttle position sensor. 14 years of heat cycling have taken their tolls, however, and the steel screws were thoroughly seized in the aluminum throttle body. Both of them broke off with just a screw driver.<P>Can I get a throttle body from any 2.8/3.1/3.4 V6 to use in place of the original while I drill out these screws?<BR>If not, what throttle bodies will work?||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||08-26-2001||07:19 PM||||I'm not sure if the motor is identical or not, but the old Cavalier Z24's came with the same intake on top.<P>There aren't to many around that will work as a direct fit.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Will||08-28-2001||08:41 PM||||Top||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dave Gunsul||08-28-2001||09:51 PM||||You can buy a used Fiero t-body from a lot<BR>of different places.<P>Paul Vargyas should have one. His email has changed to: paul@hotwires.com<P>You could even get one from Darrel Morse that's bored out: morse86@aol.com<P>Or Twin Lakes Fiero: don't remeber his website but you can link through NIFE's<BR>web-site at: <A HREF="http://www.fierofocus.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fierofocus.com</A> <P>There's also Kick Hill Farms: <A HREF="http://www.kickhill.com" TARGET=_blank>www.kickhill.com</A> <P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000004||Joe Torma||08-28-2001||10:56 PM||||You could always drill out the busted bolts and tap new holes...I had to do this to my old t-body<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Mickey_Moose||08-28-2001||11:11 PM||||I just had this happen to myself...all I did was flatten the bolt off were it broke, center punched it, drilled it out completely, used a M6 0.80 tap and cleaned out the treads - forgot which size of drill bit I used, maybe someone else here has the chart for drill bit size vs screw size (M6 in this case)<P>Tim||||reg||1
Z||000006||Standard||08-29-2001||02:12 AM||||AFAIK, the Fiero throttle body is unique, which is why it was made by Holley.  Pictures I've seen of the 2.8's from caveliers/berretta's etc have 3 vacuum lines coming from the top of the t/b.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">        <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<P><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Will||09-05-2001||09:42 PM||||I can drill it out, but I was hoping to find one to swap in so that I could drill it out at my leisure.||||reg||1
Z||000008||terryk||09-06-2001||12:46 AM||||All Code 9, W and S engines are the same except for:<P>The top plenum<BR>TB (Holley or Rochester) <BR>Mass or map<P>The accessories, exhaust and mounts are different depending on the chassis.<P>Most of the parts from the 85-87 A and X engines are the same.<P>Am I crazy or did the first year Beretta use the Holley TB? I might have been under the influence....<BR><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 09-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||artherd||09-06-2001||04:55 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Will:<BR><B>I can drill it out, but I was hoping to find one to swap in so that I could drill it out at my leisure.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Will, I've got a whole crappy arse v6 with rod knock from the car that the northstar is going into, want the TB off it before I toss it off a cliff?  Toss me an email.<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
